<figure class="flex flex-col gap-4 border-2 border-ink p-4 sm:p-6">
<p class="font-bold">Two identical capacitors share charge, but only half the initial energy remains stored.</p>
<div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-base"><div class="border-2 border-ink p-3"><strong>Before connecting</strong><p>Capacitor 1: voltage V</p><p>Capacitor 2: empty</p><p class="mt-2 font-bold">Stored energy = ½CV²</p></div><div class="border-2 border-ink p-3"><strong>After settling</strong><p>Each capacitor: voltage V/2</p><p>Each holds half the charge</p><p class="mt-2 font-bold">Total energy = ¼CV²</p></div></div>
<svg viewBox="0 0 460 110" class="w-full" role="img" aria-labelledby="capacitor-title capacitor-desc"><title id="capacitor-title">Half the initial stored energy transfers outside the capacitors</title><desc id="capacitor-desc">Of the initial energy, one half remains in the two capacitors and one half transfers via the connecting circuit and fields.</desc>
<rect x="18" y="20" width="424" height="34" fill="#d7a13d"/>
<rect x="18" y="20" width="212" height="34" fill="#387a91"/>
<g fill="currentColor" font-size="17"><text x="18" y="14">Initial energy</text><text x="18" y="84">½ remains stored</text><text x="260" y="84">½ leaves the capacitors</text></g></svg>
<figcaption class="text-base leading-normal">Each final capacitor stores ½C(V/2)², so together they store ¼CV²: half the original ½CV². The other half is transferred to heating, electromagnetic fields or radiation during the current flow. An ideal resistance-free circuit cannot simply be assumed to settle instantly into that static state.</figcaption></figure>